WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.490
If there is one thing fans like more than
watching their favorite movies, it's ranking

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:05.890
every aspect of them.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:11.330
"The Batman," the latest in a storied history
of Batman movies, provides fresh fodder for

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.330
fans.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.650
So the real question is: Pattinson vs. Bale.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.010
Who really played the better Batman?

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.220
The Dark Knight has been played by so many
actors at this point that you would be hard-pressed

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:25.119
to find a person who doesn't have some sort
of ranking for the collection of actors and

00:00:25.119 --> 00:00:26.609
their respective portrayals.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.539
It used to be that a favorite Batman could
be separated by generation.

00:00:30.539 --> 00:00:35.640
It's now more apt to compare Batman performances
based on intention and tone than anything

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.550
else, especially when you consider the thematic
valleys between, say, George Clooney in "Batman

00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.190
&amp; Robin" and Ben Affleck in "Batman v Superman:
Dawn of Justice."

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:48.730
Some of the performances, however, are easy
to compare, arguably the two closest being

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.210
Christian Bale and Robert Pattinson.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.030
Bale portrayed Batman in Christopher Nolan's
famed "Dark Knight" trilogy, while Robert

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.469
Pattinson debuted his version of the caped
crusader in this year's "The Batman."

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:03.390
Both depictions of Batman examine the early
years of the vigilante through a lens far

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.810
more grounded in reality than other more fantastical
comic book movies.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:12.229
But which actor do fans think did a better
job bringing a darker Dark Knight to life?

00:01:12.229 --> 00:01:16.389
Director Christopher Nolan's "Batman Begins"
became one of the most critically acclaimed

00:01:16.389 --> 00:01:21.390
comic book films ever when it was released
in 2005, winning near-universal praise from

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.389
both critics and fans.

00:01:23.389 --> 00:01:27.560
Fans have continued to show support for Bale,
with the actor even being voted the best Batman

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.099
in a poll this year from GameSpot.

00:01:29.099 --> 00:01:35.749
Out of more than 290,000 votes, Bale received
66% of the support as the best Batman against

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:39.060
competitors Ben Affleck, Adam West, and Michael
Keaton.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.240
While Nolan's "The Dark Knight" is the high
mark for many fans regarding "Batman" movies,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.469
some are already declaring Robert Pattinson
and "The Batman" superior even though the

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:50.820
film was only just released.

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:55.359
"I'm vengeance."

00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:59.929
Like Bale, Pattinson has also won over critics,
with "The Batman" currently standing at an

00:01:59.929 --> 00:02:02.399
85% "fresh" rating on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:06.749
Critic Christy Lemire drew comparisons to
Robert De Niro in "Taxi Driver" in her review

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:08.429
for RogerEbert.com.

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:09.429
She said:

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.900
"This is Travis Bickle in the Batsuit, detached
and disillusioned.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:18.409
[He's] not just prepared but hungry to explore
this figure's weird, dark instincts."

00:02:18.409 --> 00:02:22.000
There is plenty to compare when looking at
the performances of Christian Bale and Robert

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.670
Pattinson in their respective "Batman" projects.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:29.200
Both actors turned to edgy adaptations of
the character after careers building respectable

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.510
performances in challenging pieces.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.810
Bale performed in movies like "American Psycho"
and Pattinson more recently with indie films

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:36.969
such as "The Lighthouse."

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:41.849
Both have also earned similar praise for their
debut portrayals of Batman, a character each

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:46.410
shows as a brooding figure at the beginning
of a journey of possible addiction to his

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:47.959
vigilante persona.

00:02:47.959 --> 00:02:50.379
Between the two, however, Bale is the favorite.

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:54.260
This may not always be the case, but with
three highly praised movies under his belt,

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.640
Bale has earned more faith with audiences.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.440
"What the hell are you?"

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.360
"I'm Batman."

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.220
Next to the recent GameSpot poll crowning
Bale as the fans' favorite by a wide margin,

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:13.230
there is also a 2020 survey similarly finding
Bale on the top of the Batman heap.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:18.030
While "The Batman" has earned plenty of praise
too, Bale's movies remain more universally

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:22.450
liked, with "The Dark Knight" touching 94%
with critics and audiences alike on Rotten

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:23.500
Tomatoes.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:27.310
Even "The Dark Knight Rises" earned higher
marks with critics than "The Batman."

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.840
While Pattinson has not dethroned Bale, it
should be noted that "The Batman" is only

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.659
his first film, and he hasn't been included
in many public polls.

00:03:34.659 --> 00:03:38.950
If the reviews are any indication, though,
Pattinson could soon be replacing Bale for

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.110
many as their preferred Dark Knight.

